WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.420
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:15.983
Unit thirty: Future in the Past. Today you will describe plans and expectations from a past viewpoint.

4
00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:18.807
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:23.046
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:25.093
Was going to.

7
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:28.176
Was going to means a past plan.

8
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:30.202
I was going to call.

9
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:33.736
Your turn. Say: Was going to.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.775
Was going to.

11
00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:39.053
Would.

12
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:43.025
Would means used for the future from a past viewpoint.

13
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:45.117
She knew she would win.

14
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:48.067
Your turn. Say: Would.

15
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:51.540
Would.

16
00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:53.447
Was about to.

17
00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.995
Was about to means just before an action.

18
00:00:57.583 --> 00:00:58.851
I was about to leave.

19
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.951
Your turn. Say: Was about to.

20
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.115
Was about to.

21
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:07.770
Was to.

22
00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:11.433
Was to means a formal arrangement in the past.

23
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:13.471
He was to arrive at noon.

24
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:16.770
Your turn. Say: Was to.

25
00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:20.634
Was to.

26
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:22.164
Plan.

27
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.813
Plan means an intention.

28
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:26.778
My plan failed.

29
00:01:27.383 --> 00:01:29.734
Your turn. Say: Plan.

30
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.369
Plan.

31
00:01:34.117 --> 00:01:35.095
Prediction.

32
00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:38.408
Prediction means a guess about what would happen.

33
00:01:39.017 --> 00:01:40.447
The prediction was right.

34
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.517
Your turn. Say: Prediction.

35
00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.321
Prediction.

36
00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:49.293
Unfulfilled.

37
00:01:50.283 --> 00:01:52.933
Unfulfilled means not done or not achieved.

38
00:01:53.517 --> 00:01:55.226
An unfulfilled plan.

39
00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:58.457
Your turn. Say: Unfulfilled.

40
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.464
Unfulfilled.

41
00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:04.229
Narrative.

42
00:02:05.217 --> 00:02:06.926
Narrative means a story.

43
00:02:07.517 --> 00:02:09.214
The narrative continues.

44
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:12.748
Your turn. Say: Narrative.

45
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.648
Narrative.

46
00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:21.607
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:26.203
Visal, tell me something you were going to do yesterday but did not do.

48
00:02:27.317 --> 00:02:35.391
I was going to call my grandmother, but I forgot. Was going to shows a past plan, and it often means that the plan did not happen.

49
00:02:36.483 --> 00:02:38.251
What other forms exist?

50
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:53.664
Would: She knew that she would win. Was about to: I was about to leave when the phone rang. Was to: The president was to arrive at noon. These forms look at the future from a past point of view.

51
00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:55.960
Why are they useful?

52
00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:08.955
In stories and reports we describe what people planned, expected or predicted. The future in the past is common in narratives: He didn't know he would never return.

53
00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.565
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.417 --> 00:03:17.551
Grammar focus: Future in the past: was going to, would, was about to, was to.

55
00:03:17.851 --> 00:03:19.015
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.717 --> 00:03:21.681
I was going to call my grandmother.

57
00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:23.910
She knew she would win.

58
00:03:24.817 --> 00:03:26.932
I was about to leave when the phone rang.

59
00:03:27.867 --> 00:03:36.945
Was going to = past plan (often not done). Would = prediction from the past. Was about to = just before. Was to = formal arrangement.

60
00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:41.218
Be careful! Don't say: I will call you, but I forgot.

61
00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.816
Say: I was going to call you, but I forgot.

62
00:03:46.116 --> 00:03:47.373
Use was going to.

63
00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:50.726
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:52.848
Plans That Changed.

65
00:03:53.148 --> 00:03:55.705
I was going to call my grandmother, but I forgot.

66
00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.688
She knew that she would win the prize.

67
00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.001
We were about to leave when the phone rang.

68
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.860
The president was to arrive at noon.

69
00:04:05.867 --> 00:04:08.493
An unfulfilled plan makes a good story.

70
00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.462
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.317 --> 00:04:16.560
I blank call you, but I forgot.

72
00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.595
A, was going to. B, am going to. C, will.

73
00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:26.237
The answer is A: was going to.

74
00:04:27.383 --> 00:04:29.453
He knew he blank pass the test.

75
00:04:29.753 --> 00:04:32.640
A, will. B, is. C, would.

76
00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.909
The answer is C: would.

77
00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.713
We blank leave when it rained.

78
00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:44.933
A, were about to. B, are about to. C, will.

79
00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.431
The answer is A: were about to.

80
00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:53.386
Which shows a formal arrangement?

81
00:04:53.686 --> 00:04:58.477
A, He is arriving.. B, He arrives.. C, He was to arrive at noon..

82
00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:04.462
The answer is C: He was to arrive at noon..

83
00:05:05.617 --> 00:05:08.510
According to the reading, why did the writer not call?

84
00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:12.510
A, forgot. B, was busy. C, was ill.

85
00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:17.857
The answer is A: forgot.

86
00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:22.218
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:23.083 --> 00:05:27.010
Write a sentence about something you were going to do yesterday but did not do.

88
00:05:35.817 --> 00:05:37.305
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:37.605 --> 00:05:47.203
I was going to go jogging yesterday, but it rained. I was about to leave when the storm started. I use was going to because the plan was not completed.

90
00:05:47.503 --> 00:05:49.270
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:57.097
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future in the past: was going to, would, was about to, was to.

92
00:05:57.397 --> 00:06:01.686
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:01.986 --> 00:06:04.545
See you in Unit thirty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:06:04.845 --> 00:06:07.800
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

